{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And in the vine were three branches.</b> Shoots, from the language of (Joel 1:7) הלבינו שריגיה. <b>And it was as though it budded.</b> That is, as soon as it budded, its blossom went up. As soon as it began to bud, its blossom went up and the blossom emerged from the vine, and this is the סמדר (the unripe cluster), in the language of (Song of Songs 7:13) אם פרחה הגפן; and afterward it opened the סמדר, and immediately its blossom went up, which is the סמדר, and immediately he saw that its clusters ripened into grapes. Now this dream indicates that Elohim acts swiftly to bring a matter about, for as soon as the vine budded, immediately came the blossom and the completion of the fruit, and he pressed the grapes and brought out the wine and placed it on the cup of Pharaoh — and because he saw the budding of the vine and the opening of the סמדר and the ripening of the grapes, which were events following one after another in rapid succession, indicating urgency and the speed of the matter, therefore Yosef saw in his wisdom to interpret the three branches as three days to bring the time near, and he did not interpret three months or years. And the word שריגים is from the language of the Rabbis of blessed memory: שרגא, which is a word for light, and the same applies to שלשה סלי חורי, which he also interpreted as three days, even though its plain sense means חררה (white bread); and further it includes light and whiteness from the root חיור; and thus the Rabbis of blessed memory expounded (Exodus 33:23) וראית את אחורי as from the word for light; and similarly the phrase חורים וסגנים — for Scripture likens the great in rank to the rank of light, and the lowly who have no rank it likens to darkness and calls them חשוכים, as it is written (Proverbs 22:29) בל יתיצב לפני חשכים. And furthermore, the three baskets amount to the number three days." "<b>And further,</b> one may explain that Yosef saw fit to interpret three branches and three baskets of white bread as three days and not months or years, because he saw the branches and the baskets as identical to one another, and this can only be in days alone, for the months — you will not find three months in all the year that are completely identical, but they change and alternate from seedtime to harvest, from cold to heat, and from summer to winter; and you will not find them identical except in days. And on account of the equality found in three days, unlike three months and all the more so three years, therefore he saw fit to interpret for them an interpretation of days, and said: three days they are." "<b>By way of the Midrash:</b> ובגפן שלשה שריגים — 'vine,' this is Israel, as it is said (Psalms 80:9) גפן ממצרים תסיע. 'Three branches,' these are the three pilgrim festivals on which Israel go up every year. 'And it was as though it budded' — the time had come for Israel to be fruitful and multiply, and so it says (Exodus 1:7) ובני ישראל פרו וישרצו. 'Its blossom went up' — the time had come for Israel to be redeemed, and so Scripture says (Isaiah 63:3) ויז נצחם על בגדי. 'Its clusters ripened into grapes' — the time of Egypt had come to drink the cup of reeling, and so you will find in the parashah 'cup' four times, corresponding to the four cups of Passover, and corresponding to them the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to make the wicked drink four cups of calamity, as it is said (Jeremiah 25:15) קח את כוס היין החמה הזאת מידי. And it is written: כוס זהב בבל ביד ה'. And it is written (Psalms 75:9) כי כוס ביד ה' ויין חמר מלא מסך. And it is written (ibid. 11) ימטר על רשעים פחים אש וגפרית ורוח זלעפות מנת כוסם." "<b>And further,</b> the Rabbis of blessed memory expounded <b>And in the vine were three branches:</b> <b>Vine</b> — this is Torah. <b>Three branches</b> — this is the Well, and the Pillar of Cloud, and the Manna. <b>And it was as though it budded, its blossom went up</b> — these are first fruits. <b>Its clusters ripened into grapes</b> — these are libations."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {2 "The citation 'וכתיב כוס זהב בבל ביד ה׳' is written without a verse reference in the source; it alludes to Jeremiah 51:7. The fourth 'cup' in the parashah and its exact loci are left as he gives them."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:20.356843327Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}